    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes with the test green. The audit log confirms the new identity in action: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence entirely.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 Replaced `forSequence(city, lastName, sequence)` with `forRegionAndIdentity(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)`, which assembles `region + \"-\" + HASH8`, where HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` (reusing the existing `Sha256` helper).\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.buildCustomerCode`** \u2014 Now derives the region from the postcode (falling back to city) via `OwnerLocality.forPostcodeAndCity` and passes the normalized telephone + last name to the new `CustomerCode` method. Removed the sequence lookup.\n\n3. **`OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Added `forCustomerCode(customerCode)`, which returns the REGION segment (before the first `-`), so locality is now derived from the identity rather than re-derived independently (null-safe \u2192 `\"UNKNOWN\"`).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 The `locality` mapping now derives from `owner.getCustomerCode()` instead of postcode/city.\n\n**Values that \"moved\" automatically** (they already reference `customerCode`, so they inherit the new identity with no logic change):\n- **membershipNumber** = `customerCode + \"-M\" + YY`\n- **checkDigit** = Luhn over the digits of `customerCode` (now the hex digits of HASH8)\n- **audit record** = logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions/examples for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality`, plus a stale comment in `LuhnCheckDigit`, to match the new format.\n\nThe full suite runs green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
